rse.rs"]}], "tests": ["datetime::tests::test_datetime_from_str"]}, "shard": "chrono", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix arbitrary string slicing in `parse_rfc3339_relaxed`", "summary": "The relaxed RFC3339 parser slices the timezone suffix at byte 3 while checking for UTC, panicking when that index splits a UTF-8 character. The fix compares bytes instead, allowing malformed suffixes to return a parse error. The fix adds an assertion to test_datetime_from_str that rejects \"2015-02-18T23:16:9.15\u00f8\u00f8\u00f8\"; reversing the implementation line should make this assertion panic during parsing. No tests were executed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:05:17.598563+00:00"}
